  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The ellipse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;passes through the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>On solving equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>We know that, focii of the ellipse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#177;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Its focus is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, equation of circle is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Solving <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math> we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
